<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<class name="ColorScheme" inherits="Resource" api_type="core" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="../../../doc/class.xsd">
	<brief_description>
		Generates a semantic color palette from a source color or texture.
	</brief_description>
	<description>
		Generates light or dark semantic colors from [member source_color] or the representative color of [member source_texture]. Colors can be requested by [enum ColorRole] with [method get_color], or through the role-specific getter methods.
		The generated palette updates synchronously when a source, [member dark], or [member contrast_level] changes. The new colors are available before the setter returns and before [signal updated_color_scheme] and [signal Resource.changed] are emitted. Consumers may process their own theme notifications later.
		[Theme], [Control], [Window], [ColorRect], and dynamic [StyleBox] properties can use this resource to recolor an interface while retaining static fallback colors.
	</description>
	<tutorials>
	</tutorials>
